$ grep -n -A6 "How the merge branch affects your workflow" events.md
472:### How the merge branch affects your workflow
473-
474-For open, mergeable pull requests, workflows triggered by the `pull_request` event set `GITHUB_REF` to the merge branch. Because `actions/checkout` uses `GITHUB_REF` by default, it checks out the merge branch. Your CI tests run against the merged result, not just the head branch alone:
475-
476-* `GITHUB_REF` is set to `refs/pull/PULL_REQUEST_NUMBER/merge`
477-* `GITHUB_SHA` is the SHA of the merge commit on the merge branch
478-
479-To test only the head branch commits without simulating a merge, check out the head branch using `github.event.pull_request.head.sha` in your workflow.
480-
